%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a407502170d34004ba29f843c41175d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: PendulumConfig_Azm
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::VirtualLab.Azm.Pendulum.PendulumConfig_Azm
  trueGravity: 9.8
  oscillationCount: 20
  minimumLengths: 5
  bobDiameterCm: 2
  useCaliperStep: 1
  minLengthCm: 30
  maxLengthCm: 100
  lengthResolutionCm: 0.1
  startingLengthCm: 60
  minLengthSeparationCm: 2
  maxReleaseAngleDeg: 15
  minReleaseAngleDeg: 3
  maxDragAngleDeg: 35
  pushSpeedThresholdDegPerSec: 45
  offMeanAngleFraction: 0.65
  halfSwingIntervalRatio: 0.7
  halfSwingMinIntervals: 3
  missedCountIntervalRatio: 1.6
  originInterceptFraction: 0.1
  steps:
  - id: 0
    instruction: Bob diameter d = 2.00 cm (given)
    why: "With d given, r = d/2 = 1.00 cm. The bob swings about its centre, so the
      effective length is L = \u2113 + r."
    view: 0
    controls: 1
    drawer: 0
    guideProcedureIndex: 1
  - id: 8
    instruction: Measure the bob's diameter d
    why: "The thread length \u2113 is measured to the TOP of the bob, but the bob
      swings about its centre. You need the radius r = d/2 to get the real (effective)
      length L = \u2113 + r."
    view: 3
    controls: 64
    drawer: 3
    guideProcedureIndex: 1
  - id: 1
    instruction: "Drag the bob to set the length \u2113"
    why: "You time the pendulum at several different lengths, then plot T\xB2 against
      L. Each length gives one point on the graph."
    view: 1
    controls: 2
    drawer: 3
    guideProcedureIndex: 2
  - id: 2
    instruction: "Pull the bob aside (\u2264 15\xB0), let go"
    why: "Only small swings (15\xB0 or less) are simple harmonic motion, where T
      = 2\u03C0\u221A(L/g) holds. Let go from rest - a push adds energy."
    view: 1
    controls: 0
    drawer: 0
    guideProcedureIndex: 4
  - id: 3
    instruction: Tap at the centre, then each full swing
    why: 'Timing 20 oscillations, not one, spreads your reaction-time error over
      20 swings. Start and stop at the centre: the bob is fastest there, so the moment
      is easiest to judge.'
    view: 2
    controls: 4
    drawer: 0
    guideProcedureIndex: 5
  - id: 4
    instruction: Time 20 oscillations again
    why: Two runs averaged reduce the effect of one badly timed run.
    view: 2
    controls: 4
    drawer: 0
    guideProcedureIndex: 8
  - id: 5
    instruction: Row recorded - add another length
    why: The syllabus asks for at least 5 different lengths, so the graph has enough
      points to show a straight line.
    view: 1
    controls: 24
    drawer: 1
    guideProcedureIndex: 10
  - id: 6
    instruction: "Check your graph: T\xB2 against L"
    why: "T\xB2 = (4\u03C0\xB2/g) L, so T\xB2 against L is a straight line through
      the origin with slope 4\u03C0\xB2/g. That gives g = 4\u03C0\xB2 / slope."
    view: 0
    controls: 32
    drawer: 2
    guideProcedureIndex: 13
  - id: 7
    instruction: Your result
    why: 
    view: 0
    controls: 0
    drawer: 3
    guideProcedureIndex: 14
